<title>GERMANY: German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government is lowering the yield on its five-year Bundesobligationen bonds by raising the issue price of the paper to 101.50 from 101.20, the Bundesbank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The move brings the yield on the Series 121 paper to 4.39 percent from 4.47 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
